The action of $lr(chevron.l sigma chevron.r)$ on ${1, ..., n}$ partitions the set into orbits. Choosing one representative $i_j$ from each orbit gives
$
  sigma = product_j mat(i_j, sigma(i_j), ..., sigma^(n_j - 1)(i_j)),
$
where $n_j$ is the size of the orbit of $i_j$. Changing an orbit representative cyclically shifts its cycle, and changing the order of the orbits reorders the cycles.
